   "id": "e1",
   "source_id": "exr:3.8.1",
   "source_number": "Exercise 3.8.1",
   "kind": "exercise",
   "bloom": "Apply",
   "place": {
    "at": "end"
   },
   "cite": "the-uncertainty-principle",
   "prompt": "<p>A particle is in a state described by the ground state wavefunction of a particle in a box</p>\n$$ \\psi = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{2}{L}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{L}\\right) $$\n<p>where $L$ is the length of the box and $0\\le x \\le L$. Verify that the value of the product $\\Delta p\\Delta x$ is consistent with the predictions from the uncertainty principle (Equation 3.8.8).</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "number",
    "value": 0.568,
    "unit": "ħ",
    "tol": 0.01,
    "hint": "You need $\\langle x^2 \\rangle$ and $\\langle p^2 \\rangle$; $\\langle x \\rangle$ and $\\langle p \\rangle$ come from Section 3.7.",
    "solution": "<p>For the box the density is symmetric about the center, so $\\langle x \\rangle = L/2$, and $\\langle p \\rangle = 0$ (Example 3.7.3). The other two averages are</p>$$ \\langle x^2 \\rangle = \\dfrac{2}{L}\\int_0^L x^2 \\sin^2\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{L}\\right)dx = L^2\\left(\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{1}{2\\pi^2}\\right) $$$$ \\langle p^2 \\rangle = -\\hbar^2\\dfrac{2}{L}\\int_0^L \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{L}\\right)\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{L}\\right)dx = \\dfrac{\\pi^2\\hbar^2}{L^2} $$<p>so, by Equations 3.8.2 and 3.8.3,</p>$$ \\Delta x = L\\sqrt{\\dfrac{1}{12} - \\dfrac{1}{2\\pi^2}} = 0.181\\,L $$$$ \\Delta p = \\dfrac{\\pi\\hbar}{L} $$$$ \\Delta p\\,\\Delta x = \\hbar\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\pi^2}{12} - \\dfrac{1}{2}} = 0.568\\,\\hbar $$<p>The box length cancels, and $0.568\\,\\hbar$ is larger than $\\hbar/2$, so the product agrees with Equation 3.8.8. Unlike the Gaussian of Example 3.8.1, the ground state of the box does not reach the equality.</p>",
    "generated_by": "ai"
   }
  }
 ],
